questions.explanation:
**Given:**

Rope length = 20 m

Angle with ground = 60&deg;

**Formula Used:**

Height = Hypotenuse × sin&theta;

Base = Hypotenuse × cos&theta;

**Calculation:**

&rArr; Height = 20 × sin60&deg;

&rArr; Height = 20 × (√3 &divide; 2)

&rArr; Height = 10√3 &asymp; 17.32 m

&rArr; Base = 20 × cos60&deg;

&rArr; Base = 20 × (1 &divide; 2)

&rArr; Base = 10 m

**&there4; The correct answer is 17.32 m and 10 m.**

